# Plugin Architecture: Subprocess-Based CLAP Hosting

## Overview

- Each CLAP plugin runs in its own subprocess for crash isolation, GUI compatibility, and sandboxing.
- Engine-side code speaks to the subprocess through TCP IPC and shared-memory ring buffers; `SubprocessClapAdapter` is the AudioDevice entry point.

## Key Components

- `subprocess_adapter.rs`: Manages async lifecycle, shared memory handles, and engine-visible state.
- `process_manager.rs`: Spawns the subprocess, creates `memfd` regions, and passes FDs over Unix sockets.
- `shared_memory.rs` + `platform_shm.rs`: Lock-free audio/MIDI ring buffers backed by the shared `memfd`.
- `plugin_host.rs`: Subprocess executable; runs CLAP plugin, host extensions, and IPC loop.

## Audio Thread Contract

- Never block, allocate, or take contended locks on the audio thread; prefer `try_lock()` and skip work if unavailable.
- Check ring-buffer capacity before read/write; treat return values defensively because IPC peers may lag.

## Lifecycle

- Adapter loads plugins on a background thread and transitions Loading → Ready → Failed; expose audio only when Ready.
- Shared memory FD is sent via `SCM_RIGHTS`; clear `FD_CLOEXEC` before fork so the child can mmap it.
- Losing the TCP connection indicates a dead subprocess—mark Failed and drop the device.

## IPC Commands

- Engine issues Initialize, Activate, StartProcessing, Shutdown, Reset, OpenGui/CloseGui.
- `SetParameter`/`OpenGui`/`Reset` must be fire-and-forget from the engine; the subprocess denormalizes parameter values and calls `params.flush()` immediately so edits apply even while audio is stopped.
- `GetParameterInfo` and `GetParameter` expect responses; only non-audio threads should call them.

## Parameter Handling

- Engine ↔ Godot use normalized 0.0–1.0 values; convert with min/max stored in `ParamInfo`.
- Cache parameter metadata in `Arc<Mutex<Vec<ParamInfo>>>` before signaling Ready so UI consumers receive a complete list.
- Value queries grab the subprocess with `try_lock()` and a short timeout to avoid starving realtime work.

## GUI Support

- The subprocess implements CLAP HostGui + HostTimer; the event loop ticks timers (~1 ms) and runs `on_main_thread_callback()` to keep plugin windows responsive.

## Monitoring

- Treat subprocess exit or IPC timeouts as fatal; clean up shared memory and transition to Failed.
- When debugging, verify the subprocess binary is running and still holds the shared-memory FD (see `/proc/<pid>/fd/3`).
